values.content:
Design an onboarding email sequence.

Product: {{ $json.productName }}
Description: {{ $json.productDescription || 'not provided' }}
Target persona: {{ $json.targetPersona }}
Sequence length: {{ $json.sequenceLengthDays }} days
Number of emails: {{ $json.emailsInSequence }}
Tone: {{ $json.tone.replace(/_/g,' ') }}

Key activation actions (in order of importance):
{{ $json.keyActions.map((a,i)=>(i+1)+'. '+a).join('\n') }}

Activation goal: {{ $json.activationGoal }}

Known drop-off reasons:
{{ $json.commonDropoffReasons || 'not specified' }}

Existing engagement data:
{{ $json.existingEngagementData || 'none available' }}

Return JSON:
{"sequence_strategy":"2-3 sentences on the strategic approach — what this sequence optimizes for and why","emails":[{"email_number":1,"send_day":0,"trigger":"immediate|day_N|action_based","subject_line":"the email subject","preview_text":"under 90 chars","goal":"what this email should get the user to do","opening_line":"first sentence — hooks attention without being generic","body_outline":"3-5 bullet points of what the email covers","cta_text":"the single call to action","cta_destination":"where CTA links","personalization_tokens":["merge tags or dynamic content to include"],"skip_if":"condition under which this email should be suppressed — e.g. user already completed action"}],"a_b_test_suggestions":["specific things worth testing in this sequence"],"success_metrics":["what to measure to know if this sequence is working"]}
